{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0053"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c005): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c005.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0053"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/motor-winter","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__motor-winter.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",64],["-","water"],["+","water,"],["=",1],["-","and, most recently, "],["=",8],["-","wheels."],["+","wheels and, most recently, even the air."],["=",267],["-","1965"],["+","1965,"],["=",1],["+","two skis tied together, "],["=",229],["+"," Lying down works too: in 1971 the surfer Tom Morey, living in Hawaii, cut a light foam board and called it the Boogie Board, the ancestor of every bodyboard."],["=",151],["+","The boldest idea leaves the ground altogether. Wingboarding, a trend sport presented in 2014 by the American Aaron Wypyszynski, puts the rider on a winged board that is towed through the air behind a light aircraft, just as a wakeboarder is pulled behind a boat; so far it is more prototype than mass sport.\n\n"],["=",113],["+","\n| Boogie Board | waves | invented 1971 |\n| Wingboard | air | presented 2014 |"],["=",48]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",62],["-","Wasser"],["+","Wasser,"],["=",1],["-","und zuletzt "],["=",6],["-","Räder."],["+","Räder und zuletzt sogar die Luft."],["=",269],["-","1965"],["+","1965,"],["=",1],["+","zwei zusammengebundenen Skiern, "],["=",223],["+"," Auch im Liegen geht es: 1971 schnitt der auf Hawaii lebende Surfer Tom Morey ein leichtes Brett aus Schaumstoff zurecht und nannte es Boogie Board – der Urahn aller Bodyboards."],["=",149],["+","Am weitesten geht eine Idee, die den Boden ganz verlässt. Beim Wingboarden, einer 2014 vom Amerikaner Aaron Wypyszynski vorgestellten Trendsportart, steht der Fahrer auf einem geflügelten Brett, das von einem Leichtflugzeug durch die Luft gezogen wird, so wie ein Wakeboarder vom Boot; bislang ist es eher Prototyp als Massensport.\n\n"],["=",113],["+","\n| Boogie Board | Wellen | erfunden 1971 |\n| Wingboard | Luft | vorgestellt 2014 |"],["=",48]]}]},
